  "source": "PLAN §8.5 and §10 conversation subset (R-01); prototype Nouri App.dc.html SCRIPT and FINAL",
  "rules": {
    "walk": "Turns run in order. A turn is asked when at least one of its questions is applicable (branching rules in questions.v3.json) and is not answered or skipped yet. Otherwise it is skipped silently.",
    "skipWhen": "When a turn's skipWhen condition is true the whole turn is skipped, even if a question in it would otherwise be asked. Same grammar as questions.v1.json conditionGrammar.",
    "partialAnswers": "If a reply answers only some questions in the group, Milo asks the rest one at a time with askOne lines before moving to the next turn. A question the user declines is saved as skipped and never asked again in this conversation.",
    "provisional": "q09 is listed on the body turn so one reply can give height and weight together: its rule needs q08, so the server holds it until q08 is saved. Volunteered answers to later questions are held the same way and saved when their rules show them.",
    "lineComposition": "Milo's spoken line = the model's short ack (max 1 sentence) + the canonical miloLine or askOne text from this file. Canonical lines are pre-rendered as audio under tts/{version}/conversation.turnN.mp3.",
    "chips": "Chips are equal to voice and typed replies. A chip with sets saves those answers directly (inputMethod chip, confidence 1) without a model call. A chip with skips saves those questions as skipped.",
    "confirmation": "Every turn that extracts more than one answer, and every answer with confidence below 0.7, shows the confirm step before anything is saved (PLAN §8.5.4).",
    "sensitive": "q06, q07, q08, q09 and q38 MUST come from an explicit statement in this conversation. Never infer them from a name, voice, photo or other answers. q07 and q38 are always their own turn with chips, even by voice.",
    "deferred": "Skip to my plan, or reaching the end, opens Review. Every applicable question not answered or skipped here is stored as deferred and drives the Finish setting up card; questions that do not apply are stored as not_applicable.",
    "degraded": "If extraction returns AI_UNAVAILABLE, show Milo line onboarding.degraded and open the manual form at the current turn's first unanswered question with the answers so far.",
    "volunteered": "A reply may answer questions from later turns (never q07 or q38, which are always asked). Those answers are saved, so Milo never asks them again.",
    "sync": "The server is the source of truth during the conversation. The app uploads its local answers before the walk starts and takes the server state again before Review or the manual form."
  },
